[{"category":"section","location":"#EnergyMinimizingDD.jl","page":"Home","text":"EnergyMinimizingDD.jl contains the Julia implementation and numerical experiments for the accompanying paper on energy-minimizing domain decomposition.\n\nwarning: Project status\nEnergyMinimizingDD.jl is experimental research software. The public API may evolve before a stable release.","title":"EnergyMinimizingDD.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"From the repository root, instantiate the project environment with\n\njulia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'\n\nJulia 1.10 or newer is required.","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Reproducing-the-paper-results","page":"Home","text":"Run every retained numerical study, generate the five paper figures, and regenerate the paper table with\n\njulia --project=. examples/paper/run_all.jl\n\nFor a smaller installation smoke test, use\n\nSMALL=1 FORCE=1 julia --project=. examples/paper/run_all.jl\n\nThe small run skips the publication table because it requires the full parameter grids. See the repository README for the mapping between paper outputs and study scripts.","title":"Reproducing the paper results"},{"category":"section","location":"#Checks","page":"Home","text":"Run the focused test suite with\n\njulia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.test()'","title":"Checks"}]
